WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.600 --> 00:00:06.312
Hi! Today you ask for directions.

2
00:00:06.712 --> 00:00:11.064
Excuse me, how do I get to the station?

3
00:00:12.767 --> 00:00:15.511
You need these words:

4
00:00:15.911 --> 00:00:18.727
Go straight ahead.

5
00:00:19.127 --> 00:00:21.703
Go left.

6
00:00:22.103 --> 00:00:24.631
Go right.

7
00:00:25.031 --> 00:00:27.439
as far as the traffic lights

8
00:00:27.839 --> 00:00:30.247
at the crossroads

9
00:00:30.647 --> 00:00:32.863
on the corner

10
00:00:34.567 --> 00:00:38.271
Where are you going? With zu:

11
00:00:38.671 --> 00:00:42.087
zu dem becomes zum: to the station.

12
00:00:42.487 --> 00:00:45.711
zu der becomes zur: to the post office.

13
00:00:46.111 --> 00:00:50.631
And das? Also zum: to the cinema.

14
00:00:52.333 --> 00:00:56.853
Someone explains the way – with the imperative:

15
00:00:57.253 --> 00:00:59.853
Go straight ahead.

16
00:01:00.253 --> 00:01:02.325
And then:

17
00:01:02.725 --> 00:01:05.829
Turn left at the traffic lights.

18
00:01:07.533 --> 00:01:11.693
Listen: a tourist asks Mateo.

19
00:01:12.093 --> 00:01:14.405
Excuse me!

20
00:01:14.805 --> 00:01:17.669
How do I get to the museum?

21
00:01:18.069 --> 00:01:20.669
Go straight ahead.

22
00:01:21.069 --> 00:01:24.245
Left at the traffic lights.

23
00:01:24.645 --> 00:01:26.837
Is it far?

24
00:01:27.237 --> 00:01:30.413
No, just five minutes.

25
00:01:32.100 --> 00:01:40.844
Now you! Ask politely for the way to the post office. Then explain the way to your house.

26
00:01:52.533 --> 00:01:56.669
Great! Now you can:

27
00:01:57.069 --> 00:02:03.869
You ask for directions and understand the answer. You won't get lost anymore!

28
00:02:04.269 --> 00:02:06.389
See you soon!
